---
title: Easy Creamy Vanilla Custard (CSO)
description: 
    Want perfectly smooth custard without using a water bath or tempering eggs? 
    With perfect results and zero hassle, sous vide and steam modes make this recipe worry free. 
course: dessert
difficulty: easy
cook time: 90 minutes
prep time: 5 minutes
servings: 6
source.author: Anova Culinary
source.url: https://oven.anovaculinary.com/recipe/kffHPQ2rX40CcpZVZKWK
tags: CSO, steam
---

> Use this custard base as a start to creme brûlée, cream puffs, or even as a ridiculously good pudding, adjusting the oven temperature as needed to stiffen the custard. 

>For pourable custard sauce, decrease the oven temperature to 170°F (77°C). For firmer creme brûlée, increase the oven temperature to 184°F (84°C).

Preheat the #Convection Steam Oven{} (CSO) to 177°F (80°C) in Sous Vide (if available, or full Steam) mode.

Whisk together @sugar{1/2%cup}, @egg yolks{5}(large), @vanilla extract{1%tsp}, and @salt{1/4%tsp} in a large bowl until smooth.

Slowly whisk in @heavy cream{2%cups} until fully incorporated.

Pour the custard mixture through a fine-mesh strainer into an #oven-safe baking dish{}.
For the cooking time listed in the recipe, the custard should be about 1 inch deep in the container.
If you see that the custard is significantly deeper than 1 inch, you'll need to increase the cooking time;
use an instant-read thermometer to track when the custard reaches the oven temperature.

Transfer to the oven and cook for ~{1.5%hours} or until the custard reaches 177°F (80°C) in the center.

Whisk the cooked custard until smooth.
Pour into individual #ramekins.
Refrigerate for ~{4%hours}.

Serve with dusted cinnamon, berries, or use as part of another dessert recipe, such as creme brûlée or cream puffs.
